WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.730
Impeachment is the word of the day.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.839
The first step of the impeachment process

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:11.179
of Donald Trump has started, and Donald Trump
is flying off the rails.

00:00:11.179 --> 00:00:13.639
As a result, we will talk about all of this.

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:17.119
This is an impeachment inquiry, important
word.

00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:22.781
A lot of people have very clearly not understanding
the full process, and why would you, impeachment

00:00:22.781 --> 00:00:25.140
of presidents is not a common thing.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.869
This was announced yesterday by the speaker
of the house, Nancy Pelosi.

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:29.920
Let's take a look.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:35.460
The actions of the Trump presidency revealed
dishonorable fact of the president's betrayal

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:41.360
of his oath of office, betrayal of our national
security and betrayal of the integrity of

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:42.579
our elections.

00:00:42.579 --> 00:00:47.310
Therefore, today I'm announcing the house
of representatives moving forward with an

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.649
official impeachment inquiry.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:54.399
I'm directing our six committees to proceed
with their investigations under that umbrella.

00:00:54.399 --> 00:00:55.399
So

00:00:55.399 --> 00:00:59.360
there's confusion about what this is and what
this is not.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.150
Impeachment is a long process.

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:06.540
There are three primary steps, and these can
be subdivided into even really 10 or 12 different

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:12.050
steps, but the generality, the three primary
phases are an impeachment inquiry.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:20.800
If the inquiry leads the inquirers to decide
that actually impeaching the president via

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.810
a trial is appropriate.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:28.260
You go to an impeachment trial by the house
of representatives and after that phase is

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:33.350
complete, phase two, you go to phase three,
which is a vote in the Senate as to whether

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:37.810
or not to convict the president and thus remove
them from office.

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:43.310
Now, this is not going to lead to a conviction
of Donald Trump in the Senate, and thus the

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:44.950
removal of Donald Trump.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:47.120
The Senate is controlled by Republicans.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.680
We don't have to go through the details, but
as you know, if you've been following politics

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:56.310
for the last couple of years with some very
limited exceptions, Republicans are not interested,

00:01:56.310 --> 00:02:01.860
willing, or even remotely considering removing
this president from office.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:08.509
So the process that Democrats will now follow
must be strategic and it must be thought out

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:12.510
because Donald Trump will try and he is already
trying.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:17.370
You will see his tweets momentarily to turn
this around into, he's the victim.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:23.290
He's a martyr, just doing great things for
the United States and these witch hunt Democrats

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:25.980
won't let him just make America great again.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:33.190
So this, the, the goal here is hurt Trump
in 2020 because the impeachment process is

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:35.430
not going to remove Donald Trump.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:39.670
So that then becomes a question of, are we
confident that Democrats can carry this out

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:40.850
in the right way?

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:46.080
Is there going to be in fighting among Democrats
around this such that it will become a distraction?

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:51.290
We already saw there's this, a, a member of
Congress from Hawaii who was running for president

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:52.290
named Tulsi Gabbert.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.900
She says, she's against what Nancy Pelosi
is doing.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:03:00.630
Are we going to see conflict within the democratic
party that will allow Donald Trump to take

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:02.250
advantage of this in some way?

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:07.740
Uh, last night on I did a live stream on YouTube,
uh, about the breaking impeachment news.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:12.140
And there were a lot of people who were saying,
David, you know this talk of impeachment backfiring.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:13.460
That's a Republican talking point.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.460
No, no, no.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:20.590
I'm not talking about the process backfiring
in so far as the impeachment inquiry is not

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.490
warranted on the substance.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:27.840
Donald Trump clearly deserves, at minimum
an impeachment inquiry will not put the cart

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.840
before the horse.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:32.580
Depending on what the inquiry finds, we can
talk about whether the impeachment trial is

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:33.580
the next step.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.490
That's not what I mean when I say backfire.

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:41.910
What I mean by backfire is that if Democrats
bungled the process, if Democrats bungled

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:48.290
the PR around this, it will allow Donald Trump
to paint himself successfully as the victim

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:49.569
martyr.

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:51.770
And it will not hurt him.

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:56.540
In 2020 I've been getting emails from people
saying, David, it's over for Trump.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:01.600
Trump needs to resign and set up Mike [inaudible],
Mike Pence to pardon him the way that Richard

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:02.830
Nixon did.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:07.360
Number one, it's unlikely that Donald Trump's
ego would allow that to happen, but I don't

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:08.420
think it's necessary.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:12.420
Donald Trump is not going to be convicted
on impeachment by a Republican controlled

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:18.690
Senate before January of 2021, which is when
the next, um, uh, Congress and president would

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:19.690
be sworn in.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:25.370
So there are two ways that this can go given
that Trump won't be removed before the election.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:31.590
Number one, this doesn't work because Americans
get exhausted by 14 months of it or however

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:35.730
many months, I guess for 13 months leading
up to the election and it ends up helping

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:36.730
Donald Trump.

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:37.730
That's one way.

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:42.130
The other way it can go is that the inquiry
reveals the president's wrongdoing in such

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:49.130
a, an uh, an uncontestable way, a to such
a degree that it destroys Trump and Republicans

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:50.340
in the 2020 election.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:54.490
When we go back to bill Clinton, people like
to remind me that bill Clinton's approval

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:56.070
went up during impeachment.

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:59.240
But remember number one, bill Clinton didn't
try to interfere.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:04.590
Number two, bill Clinton had a strong economy
and number three, what was at issue were lies

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:05.660
about an affair.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:11.600
Donald Trump has engaged in borderline trader
his behavior and of course Donald Trump is

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.699
absolutely losing it on Twitter, which is
an indication that he is not going to allow

00:05:15.699 --> 00:05:19.840
this process to play out calmly in the way
that bill Clinton did.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:24.590
I've been telling you for years, if impeachment
starts, what we've seen on Twitter so far

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:28.400
by Donald Trump will be nothing compared to
what we will see.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:29.400
And it's already happening.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:34.160
Donald Trump starting to wind up yesterday
tweeting such an important day at the United

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.160
nations.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.180
So much work and so much success.

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:42.169
And the Democrats purposely had to ruin and
demean it with more breaking news, which hunt

00:05:42.169 --> 00:05:44.930
garbage so bad for our country.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:49.490
Later tweeting presidential harassment in
all caps.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:52.180
And then this morning scaling it up even more.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:56.610
Donald Trump tweeting quote, there has been
no president in the history of our Capitol

00:05:56.610 --> 00:06:00.760
C country who has been treated so badly as
I have.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:03.690
The Democrats are frozen with hatred and fear.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:05.180
They get nothing done.

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:09.520
This should never be allowed to happen to
another president, which hunt.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:15.330
So remember, Trump won't be removed by this
impeachment because once again, Republicans

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:16.970
control the Senate.

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:20.210
But Donald Trump is already losing it.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:25.530
If there were to be, I mean, listen, imagine
if Donald Trump were to be convicted and removed

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:26.580
by the Senate.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:30.320
Imagine the level of violence that we would
see happening from Trumpists.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:34.350
Uh, I, I would actually consider staying away
from public places.

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.480
I really would.

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:37.490
But in the end, that's not going to happen.

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:44.620
And the conversation has been about is the
president going to be removed and what is

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:46.610
the strategy on that basis?

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:51.840
The real question is should the president
be impeached given what we know?

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:56.550
And the answer is as far as an impeachment
inquiry, obviously yes.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:07:00.740
So this inquiry is the first step and it is
the correct step.

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:02.180
There is no question about it.

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:06.850
The political strategy around it is important
given that the Senate is not going to vote

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:14.580
to convict, but on the facts, obviously there
is a, a completely, uh, there's a completely

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:18.070
obvious case for why this impeachment inquiry
is now starting.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:20.431
And it's not only Donald Trump who's flipping
out, it's also Rudy Giuliani.

00:07:20.431 --> 00:07:20.450
Let's talk about that next.

